    <div class="info-content">

        <div class="info-updated">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-clock-rotate-left"></i>
            Last updated: 1 July 2025
        </div>

        <section id="introduction">
            <h2><span class="num">1</span> Introduction</h2>
            <p>
                The City of Johannesburg ("the City", "we", "us", or "our") is committed
                to protecting the privacy and personal information of all users of the
                Valuation Portal ("the Portal"). This Privacy Policy explains how we
                collect, use, store, and protect your personal information when you
                use the Portal to search the Valuation Roll, lodge objections or
                appeals, submit property attributes, or apply for rebates.
            </p>
            <p>
                This Policy is published in accordance with the Protection of Personal
                Information Act 4 of 2013 ("POPIA") and applies to all individuals who
                access or use the Portal, including registered account holders,
                property owners, ratepayers, and authorised representatives.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section id="information-we-collect">
            <h2><span class="num">2</span> Information We Collect</h2>
            <p>We may collect and process the following categories of personal information:</p>
            <h3>Account Information</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Full name, surname, and contact details (email address, telephone, cellphone)</li>
                <li>Identity number or passport number</li>
                <li>Login credentials and account security information</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Property &amp; Objection Information</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Property descriptions, addresses, and valuation roll references</li>
                <li>Details submitted in objection, appeal, and Section 78 query forms</li>
                <li>Property attribute submissions (e.g. number of rooms, building size, improvements)</li>
                <li>Supporting documents and evidence uploaded (e.g. proof of authorisation, photographs)</li>
                <li>Electronic signatures captured for declaration purposes</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Rebate Applications</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Municipal account numbers and billing information</li>
                <li>Information relevant to rebate eligibility (e.g. pensioner status, disability status, household composition)</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Technical Information</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>IP address, browser type, and device information</li>
                <li>Login timestamps and session activity for security and audit purposes</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="info-note">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i>
                Where your objection or rebate application relates to information
                about another person (e.g. a co-owner or household member), you
                confirm that you have the necessary consent or authority to submit
                that information on their behalf.
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="how-we-use">
            <h2><span class="num">3</span> How We Use Your Information</h2>
            <p>We use your personal information to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Create and manage your Portal account</li>
                <li>Process objections, appeals, Section 78 queries, and property attribute submissions</li>
                <li>Verify your identity and your relationship to the property in question</li>
                <li>Generate official acknowledgements, notices, and decision letters</li>
                <li>Assess and process rebate applications</li>
                <li>Communicate with you regarding the status of your submissions</li>
                <li>Maintain audit trails for administrative and legal accountability</li>
                <li>Improve the functionality, security, and performance of the Portal</li>
                <li>Comply with our legal obligations under the Local Government: Municipal Property Rates Act and related legislation</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="legal-basis">
            <h2><span class="num">4</span> Legal Basis for Processing</h2>
            <p>
                We process your personal information on the following legal grounds
                recognised under POPIA:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Performance of a public function</strong> — processing objections, appeals, and valuation roll administration in terms of the Municipal Property Rates Act 6 of 2004</li>
                <li><strong>Consent</strong> — where you voluntarily register an account or submit information through the Portal</li>
                <li><strong>Legal obligation</strong> — retaining records as required by municipal record-keeping policies and legislation</li>
                <li><strong>Legitimate interest</strong> — maintaining the security, integrity, and audit trail of the Portal</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="sharing">
            <h2><span class="num">5</span> Sharing of Information</h2>
            <p>
                Your information is accessible to authorised City of Johannesburg
                officials within the Group Finance and Valuation Services
                departments for the purposes described in this Policy. We do not
                sell or rent your personal information to third parties.
            </p>
            <p>We may share information with:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Municipal Valuers and Appeal Boards, where required to assess objections and appeals</li>
                <li>Other City of Johannesburg departments responsible for billing, rates, and property records</li>
                <li>Service providers who process data on our behalf (e.g. hosting and IT support), under strict confidentiality obligations</li>
                <li>Law enforcement or regulatory authorities, where required by law or a valid legal process</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="security">
            <h2><span class="num">6</span> Data Security</h2>
            <p>
                We implement reasonable technical and organisational measures to
                protect your personal information against loss, unauthorised access,
                alteration, or disclosure. These measures include:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Secure authentication and access control for Portal accounts and administrative systems</li>
                <li>Encrypted transmission of data between your browser and our servers</li>
                <li>Role-based access restrictions for City officials</li>
                <li>Audit logging of administrative actions on objection and appeal records</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                While we take reasonable steps to secure your information, no system
                can be guaranteed to be 100% secure. Please keep your login
                credentials confidential and notify us immediately if you suspect
                unauthorised access to your account.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section id="retention">
            <h2><span class="num">7</span> Data Retention</h2>
            <p>
                We retain personal information for as long as necessary to fulfil
                the purposes outlined in this Policy, including:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>The duration of the relevant Valuation Roll cycle and any subsequent appeal periods</li>
                <li>Periods required by municipal record-keeping policies and the National Archives and Records Service of South Africa Act</li>
                <li>Periods required to resolve disputes, audits, or legal proceedings</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                When no longer required, personal information is securely deleted or
                anonymised in accordance with our records management policies.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section id="cookies">
            <h2><span class="num">8</span> Cookies &amp; Tracking</h2>
            <p>
                The Portal uses essential cookies required for login sessions,
                security (including reCAPTCHA), and to remember your preferences
                (such as "Keep me signed in"). These cookies do not track you across
                other websites and are not used for advertising purposes.
            </p>
            <p>
                You can configure your browser to refuse cookies; however, doing so
                may prevent you from logging in or using certain features of the
                Portal.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section id="your-rights">
            <h2><span class="num">9</span> Your Rights Under POPIA</h2>
            <p>As a data subject, you have the right to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Request confirmation of whether we hold personal information about you</li>
                <li>Request access to the personal information we hold about you</li>
                <li>Request correction or updating of inaccurate, outdated, or incomplete information</li>
                <li>Request deletion of personal information that we are no longer authorised to retain</li>
                <li>Object to the processing of your personal information on reasonable grounds</li>
                <li>Lodge a complaint with the Information Regulator of South Africa</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                To exercise any of these rights, please contact our Information
                Officer using the details in section 11 below.
            </p>
            <div class="info-note">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i>
                The Information Regulator (South Africa) can be contacted at
                <a href="https://inforegulator.org.za" target="_blank" rel="noopener">inforegulator.org.za</a>
                or via email at <a href="mailto:complaints.IR@justice.gov.za">complaints.IR@justice.gov.za</a>.
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="changes">
            <h2><span class="num">10</span> Changes to This Policy</h2>
            <p>
                We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect
                changes in our practices, technology, legal requirements, or other
                operational reasons. The "Last updated" date at the top of this page
                indicates when this Policy was last revised. We encourage you to
                review this page periodically.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section id="contact">
            <h2><span class="num">11</span> Contact Us</h2>
            <p>
                If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, or wish to exercise
                any of your rights under POPIA, please contact:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Information Officer:</strong> City of Johannesburg — Property Branch: Valuation Services</li>
                <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:valuationenquiries@joburg.org.za">valuationenquiries@joburg.org.za</a></li>
                <li><strong>Address:</strong> Valuation Administrations, 1st Floor, East Wing, 66 Jorissen Street, Braamfontein, Johannesburg</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                For general enquiries about the Portal, visit our
                <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.
            </p>
        </section>

    </div>
</div>
